{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If size is larger than the length of data, yield one chunk containing all data.\n    The final chunk may be smaller than size if data length is not a multiple of size.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes or str or list): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Yields:\n        chunks of data of length size, except possibly the last one.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"chunk size must be positive\")\n\n    length = len(data)\n    if length == 0:\n        return\n\n    if size >= length:\n        yield data\n        return\n\n    for i in range(0, length, size):\n        yield data[i:i + size]\n","expected_sha256":"f6e83875c7f943741935c3f9060fdbcbf9ff51658133e11b544e1b12c93beb2a","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Fixed chunk to yield one chunk if size >= length, and to yield nothing if data is empty, so final partial chunk is kept and size larger than input yields one chunk, matching the oracle tests."}